  "reason": "The current best (config_019: multimodal, multiprofile, pca_n2000, resnet50, avgpool, weighted, acc=0.639) establishes that multiprofile + avgpool + weighted fusion is the strongest configuration family. However, all experiments so far use PCA (a linear method) for RNA encoding, while the RNA modality is the dominant signal (RNA-only 0.591 vs image-only 0.208). This experiment isolates the effect of switching the RNA encoder to scvi_n200 (a learned nonlinear representation) while holding all other settings at their best-known values. If scvi improves on PCA, it directly lifts the primary signal and should translate to higher multimodal accuracy; if not, it confirms PCA is near-sufficient and the remaining budget can focus on the image encoder (ViT-L) or other levers. With only 2 experiments left, testing the highest-impact untested variable in the proven best family is the most information-rich choice."
}

